  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[Initialise the `Document` object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#initialise-the-document-object) references a response’s `timing info` twice, but Fetch removed it in [whatwg/fetch@4c93f89](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/commit/4c93f89) (\"Inline `finalize and report timing`\"), so both references are broken:\n\n* Setting `loadTimingInfo`’s [navigation start time](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#navigation-start-time).\n* Passing it to [create the navigation timing entry](https://w3c.github.io/navigation-timing/#dfn-create-the-navigation-timing-entry).\n\nThat same commit added [extract full timing info](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#extract-full-timing-info) on the fetch controller as the replacement. The second reference is inside the \"if `navigationParams`’s fetch controller is not null\" block, which already computes `fullTimingInfo` that way, so it can presumably just use that. The first is outside that block, so it needs a bit more thought.",
